apacitor should carry a capacitor footprint and have both pins connected. The spec describes the input capacitor on BAT+ to GND as a bypass to the regulator's VIN.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(value \\\"0.1uF\\\") (footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C12-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"C12\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C12 unconnected-_C12-Pad1_ 0 0.1u\"}], \"impact\": \"The capacitor is electrically floating at one end and does nothing, so the affected decoupling or bypass point has no effect. The wrong footprint could also cause assembly problems.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}]}",
